  "summary_en": "GSA's federal regulation (41 CFR Part 102-33) governing management of US Government aircraft, covering acquisition, parts, flight program standards, safety management systems, disposal, and reporting through FAIRS. Unmanned aircraft systems are included only incidentally within the definition of aircraft; there are no AI-specific provisions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Agencies must establish Flight Program Standards covering operations, maintenance, training and safety.",
   "Agencies must implement a Safety Management System aligned with FAA guidance.",
   "Aircraft accidents and incidents must be reported to NTSB and to GSA within 14 days.",
   "Agencies must report inventory, cost and utilization data, including UAS, via FAIRS.",
   "Each agency must appoint a Senior Aviation Management Official to the Interagency Committee for Aviation Policy."
  ],
